course: dictionary
lesson: 14755
title: Proportionally: same ratio, fair size
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Proportionally is an adverb. It tells you how something changes or how something is shared. When things change proportionally, they keep the same ratio, so each amount grows or shrinks by the same scale. «If you double the recipe, increase everything proportionally.» Double the flour, the sugar and the eggs, and the cake still tastes right.
explain: The word can also mean fair and in the right size compared with something else. «The prize was shared proportionally between the three teams.» Here the teams do not get the same amount, but each gets a share that fits what it did. Ask yourself: is the answer fair for each part, in the right size? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Notice the clue words around proportionally. The sentence «If you double the recipe» tells you that amounts are growing together, so it must be about the same ratio. The sentence «shared proportionally between the three teams» tells you about fairness. The context shows you which meaning is needed.
fact: Proportionally means in the same ratio, or fairly and in the right size compared with something else.
fact: «Increase proportionally» means every part grows by the same scale, so the ratio stays the same.
fact: «Shared proportionally» means each person or team gets a fair share for its size or effort.
fact: Proportionally comes from the word proportion, which compares one part with a whole.
fact: A good check is to swap in «in the same ratio» or «fairly, in the right size» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «If you double the recipe, increase everything proportionally.» What does proportionally mean here? | *In the same ratio, so every amount grows by the same scale | Only the sugar changes | In a hurry, as fast as possible | Without using any measuring
exercise: «The prize was shared proportionally between the three teams.» What does this mean? | Each team got exactly the same amount, whatever it did | Nobody got any of the prize | *Each team got a fair share, in the right size for what it did | The prize was lost
exercise: «The map was drawn proportionally, so the lake looked the right size compared with the town.» Find and copy the adverb. | *proportionally | map | town | lake
test: A cake recipe for 4 people is doubled for 8 people. How do the amounts change? | *Proportionally, every amount doubles | Only the eggs double | Not at all | The amounts change at random
test: When two amounts change proportionally, what happens? | They change at random | Only the bigger amount changes | *They change by the same scale | One goes to zero
exam: «A map keeps distances proportionally, so 1 cm stands for 10 km.» What does proportionally show here? | *Every distance is shown at the same scale | Only the roads are drawn | Some towns are drawn bigger on purpose | The map has no scale at all
